1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,448
Monday, ten fourteen in the morning.

2
00:00:02,498 --> 00:00:06,984
A buyer orders peonies from Malika's shop, types a card, and pays.

3
00:00:07,034 --> 00:00:08,856
It takes under a minute.

4
00:00:08,906 --> 00:00:14,976
In that minute, one card number passes seven layers of security, and the buyer notices none of them.

5
00:00:15,026 --> 00:00:19,536
Since Lesson 4, each lesson has added one layer around the card zone.

6
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:24,912
This lesson follows that one card number through all of them, and shows what each one stops.

7
00:00:24,962 --> 00:00:27,120
A bank vault is the right picture.

8
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,992
A gate on the street.

9
00:00:29,042 --> 00:00:30,864
Glass at the counter.

10
00:00:30,914 --> 00:00:32,736
A guard inside.

11
00:00:32,786 --> 00:00:34,608
A safe at the back.

12
00:00:34,658 --> 00:00:37,320
Inner doors that open only with the right pass.

13
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,192
Cameras everywhere.

14
00:00:39,242 --> 00:00:41,808
And keys no single person holds.

15
00:00:41,858 --> 00:00:44,616
No layer is trusted to stop everything.

16
00:00:44,666 --> 00:00:47,352
Each one assumes the layer before it might fail.

17
00:00:47,402 --> 00:00:49,896
That idea is called defence in depth.

18
00:00:49,946 --> 00:00:52,800
Layer one is the gate: the payers' door.

19
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:56,664
The buyer's browser reaches the card zone only through this door.

20
00:00:56,714 --> 00:01:01,752
It passes the card frame's few requests, and answers not found to everything else.

21
00:01:01,802 --> 00:01:04,776
It slows any one buyer who submits too fast.

22
00:01:04,826 --> 00:01:08,664
Layer two is the glass at the counter: the card form's seals.

23
00:01:08,714 --> 00:01:11,400
The frame runs only its own two files.

24
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:13,272
A changed file does not run.

25
00:01:13,322 --> 00:01:15,504
A stranger's script is refused.

26
00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:18,576
Only the payment page its session names may hold it.

27
00:01:18,626 --> 00:01:21,624
This stops a skimmer copying the number as it is typed.

28
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:24,744
Layer three is the guard: the fraud limits.

29
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:32,280
Before any network is asked, the attempt is counted by the card's fingerprint, its first digits, the buyer's address and the shop.

30
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:35,688
Past the bank's chosen limits, the try is refused.

31
00:01:35,738 --> 00:01:38,616
This stops a thief testing stolen cards.

32
00:01:38,666 --> 00:01:41,712
Layer four is the safe: sealed numbers.

33
00:01:41,762 --> 00:01:45,360
Vault seals the number, and only the sealed value is kept.

34
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:48,696
The database refuses anything unsealed.

35
00:01:48,746 --> 00:01:52,032
The number is opened only to hand it to the card's network.

36
00:01:52,082 --> 00:01:56,544
This stops a stolen database or backup from leaking a single card.

37
00:01:56,594 --> 00:02:00,912
Layer five is the inner doors: two proofs on every call.

38
00:02:00,962 --> 00:02:04,704
When ecom asks to charge the card, it never sees the number.

39
00:02:04,754 --> 00:02:06,576
It holds only the token.

40
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:12,192
Every call it makes carries two proofs: its certificate, and its token from the login server.

41
00:02:12,242 --> 00:02:15,168
Its role allows only the operations it needs.

42
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:19,632
This stops a stranger, or a caller overstepping, from using the card.

43
00:02:19,682 --> 00:02:23,712
Layer six is the cameras: logs that never show the number.

44
00:02:23,762 --> 00:02:26,352
Every use of card data is written down.

45
00:02:26,402 --> 00:02:31,296
Every log line cuts a card number down to its first six and last four digits.

46
00:02:31,346 --> 00:02:33,528
Secrets in a log are starred out.

47
00:02:33,578 --> 00:02:35,760
Alerts carry no card data at all.

48
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:39,384
This stops the record of what happened from becoming a leak.

49
00:02:39,434 --> 00:02:41,712
Layer seven is the keyholders.

50
00:02:41,762 --> 00:02:43,728
Vault itself starts locked.

51
00:02:43,778 --> 00:02:48,192
To open it, three of five keyholders each bring their own share of the key.

52
00:02:48,242 --> 00:02:50,808
This stops one insider from taking the keys.

53
00:02:50,858 --> 00:02:53,064
Now the buyer's minute, as they saw it.

54
00:02:53,114 --> 00:02:56,112
The payment page opens, and the padlock shows.

55
00:02:56,162 --> 00:02:59,280
The frame appears and groups the number in fours.

56
00:02:59,330 --> 00:03:03,192
The buyer presses Send code, and a code arrives on their own phone.

57
00:03:03,242 --> 00:03:06,288
They confirm, and the form says "Card accepted".

58
00:03:06,338 --> 00:03:10,344
The page shows only the masked line, the network and the bank.

59
00:03:10,394 --> 00:03:12,456
ecom asks for the charge by token.

60
00:03:12,506 --> 00:03:14,328
The page says "Paid".

61
00:03:14,378 --> 00:03:18,504
Seven layers worked, and the buyer saw two fields and a button.

62
00:03:18,554 --> 00:03:21,744
Later, Timur opens the card zone's logs for that payment.

63
00:03:21,794 --> 00:03:23,760
He sees only the masked number.

64
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:26,712
He also sees who asked for what, and when.

65
00:03:26,762 --> 00:03:29,736
That night, Vault restarts after maintenance.

66
00:03:29,786 --> 00:03:31,608
It comes back locked.

67
00:03:31,658 --> 00:03:37,800
The card form refuses new cards, and an alert says a service the card zone depends on is unavailable.

68
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:41,064
It stays that way until the keyholders meet and open it.

69
00:03:41,114 --> 00:03:44,712
Timur cannot open it alone, and that is exactly the point.

70
00:03:44,762 --> 00:03:48,192
I trust no single layer, not even my favourite ones.

71
00:03:48,242 --> 00:03:50,760
One day a script slips past review.

72
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:52,632
A password leaks.

73
00:03:52,682 --> 00:03:54,792
A copy of the database escapes.

74
00:03:54,842 --> 00:04:01,080
When one layer fails, the next one still holds, for the cardholders, for shops like Malika's, and for the bank.

75
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:03,360
Next: how a merchant signs up.
